#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:6
msgid "Installation (Ubuntu)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Install the ``webots_ros2`` package and run simulation examples on "
"Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:10
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:12
msgid "**Time:** 10 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:16
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:19
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:21
msgid ""
"The ``webots_ros2`` package provides an interface between ROS 2 and Webots. "
"It includes several sub-packages, including ``webots_ros2_driver``, which "
"allows you to start Webots and communicate with it. This interface is used "
"in most of the following tutorials, so it is required to install it "
"beforehand. Other sub-packages are mainly examples that show multiple "
"possible implementations using the interface. In this tutorial, you are "
"going to install the package and learn how to run one of these examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:28
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:30
msgid ""
"It is recommended to understand basic ROS principles covered in the beginner "
"tutorials. In particular, :doc:`../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/"
"Working-with-Client-Libraries/Creating-A-Workspace/Creating-A-Workspace` "
"and :doc:`../../../ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-"
"Libraries/Creating-Your-First-ROS2-Package` are useful prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:33
msgid ""
"The Webots software should be installed in order to use the ``webots_ros2`` "
"interface. You can follow the `installation procedure <https://cyberbotics."
"com/doc/guide/installation-procedure>`_ or `build it from sources <https://"
"github.com/cyberbotics/webots/wiki/Linux-installation/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:36
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also let ``webots_ros2`` download and install Webots "
"automatically. This option appears when you launch an example of the package "
"and no Webots installation is found."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:40
msgid "Multiple Installations of Webots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:42
msgid ""
"If you have installed different versions of Webots on your computer, "
"``webots_ros2`` will look for Webots at the following locations (in this "
"order):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:44
msgid ""
"If the ``ROS2_WEBOTS_HOME`` environment variable is set, ROS 2 will use the "
"Webots in this folder, regardless of its version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:45
msgid ""
"If the ``WEBOTS_HOME`` environment variable is set, ROS 2 will use the "
"Webots in this folder, regardless of its version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:46
msgid ""
"If none of these variables is set, ``webots_ros2`` will look for Webots in "
"the default installation paths for a compatible version: ``/usr/local/"
"webots`` and ``/snap/webots/current/usr/share/webots``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:47
msgid ""
"If Webots couldn't be found, ``webots_ros2`` will show a window offering the "
"automatic installation of the latest compatible version of Webots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:50
msgid "Tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:53
msgid "1 Install ``webots_ros2``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:54
msgid ""
"You can either install the official released package, or install it from the "
"latest up-to-date sources from `Github <https://github.com/cyberbotics/"
"webots_ros2>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:58
msgid "Install ``webots_ros2`` distributed package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:60
msgid "Run the following command in a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:62
msgid "$ sudo apt-get install ros-rolling-webots-ros2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:66
msgid "Install ``webots_ros2`` from sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:68
msgid "Create a ROS 2 workspace with its ``src`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:70
msgid "$ mkdir -p ~/ros2_ws/src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:74
msgid "Source the ROS 2 environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:76
#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:114
msgid "$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:80
msgid "Retrieve the sources from Github."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:82
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws\n"
"$ git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/cyberbotics/webots_ros2."
"git src/webots_ros2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:87
msgid "Install the package dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:89
msgid ""
"$ sudo apt install python3-pip python3-rosdep python3-colcon-common-"
"extensions\n"
"$ sudo rosdep init && rosdep update\n"
"$ rosdep install --from-paths src --ignore-src --rosdistro rolling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:95
msgid "Build the package using ``colcon``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:97
msgid "$ colcon build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:101
msgid "Source this workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:103
msgid "$ source install/local_setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:108
msgid "2 Launch the ``webots_ros2_universal_robot`` example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:110
msgid "The following instructions explain how to start a provided example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:112
msgid "First source the ROS 2 environment, if not done already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:118
msgid ""
"Setting the ``WEBOTS_HOME`` environment variable allows you to start a "
"specific Webots installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:120
msgid "$ export WEBOTS_HOME=/usr/local/webots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:124
msgid ""
"If installed from sources, source your ROS 2 workspace, if not done already."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:126
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros2_ws\n"
"$ source install/local_setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:131
msgid ""
"Use the ROS 2 launch command to start demo packages (e.g. "
"``webots_ros2_universal_robot``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Integrations-and-related/Simulators/Webots/Installation-Ubuntu.rst:133
msgid "$ ros2 launch webots_ros2_universal_robot multirobot_launch.py"
msgstr ""
